      "status": "theory-motivated-assumption",
      "assumption": "The measured target density operator approximately commutes with photon-number parity. The source article reports photon subtraction from squeezed light and compares the reconstructed state with a squeezed single-photon state, but experimental imperfections may introduce parity-breaking components, so this is not a proof about the released samples.",
      "mathematical_consequence": "If [rho, Pi] = 0, then P(x|theta) = P(-x|theta) for every theta; phase-insensitive loss preserves this commutation. The H2 sign transform is therefore distributionally identical to H1 under the assumption and cannot identify which source interpretation is correct.",
      "protocol_rule": "Explanatory only: do not use this assumption to select H1, suppress H2, or authorize an H1-only verdict."
    },
